ORIGINAL WORK
-------------

"Pixel 8 Pro Case (TPU)" by JamesSF69
    https://www.printables.com/model/765202-pixel-8-pro-case-tpu
    https://www.printables.com/@JamesSF69_537205
Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.


THIS WORK
---------

This repository is a derivative of the above and is licensed under the same
terms, CC BY-SA 4.0, as ShareAlike requires.

The original design — overall form, phone cavity and its clearances, lip and
rim profile, camera bar recess and lens cutouts, port layout, and button
bumps — is JamesSF69's. This repository re-derives that geometry
parametrically in build123d by measuring the published STLs.


CHANGES MADE
------------

CC BY-SA requires that modifications be indicated. Relative to the source
models, this work:

  - re-implements the geometry as a parametric build123d program rather than
    a fixed mesh
  - corrects end walls from 2.0 mm to a uniform 3.0 mm, removing a 1 mm step
    at all four corners
  - makes the back-edge chamfer symmetric (the source chamfers -X and -Y only)
  - replaces the flash/sensor circle pair with a single stadium, removing a
    0.209 mm ligament between them that cannot be printed
  - derives back thickness from the camera bar depth plus the skin over it
  - rounds the camera recess corners
  - holds rounded-rectangle radii clear of w/2 and h/2, so exact stadiums do
    not mesh with a seam that reads as a hole
  - adds optional back lightening (square-grid and honeycomb, closed or
    open-cell), side wall vents, and port bars
  - adds preset configurations, an exported-thickness report, and a
    verification script that measures deviation against the source meshes

Attribution must be preserved in any further redistribution, and derivatives
of this work must also be licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.
